## Diagnosis

One defect, one file, one line. The failing set has a single member and a single root cause.

`tests/suite/add_test.go` (read-only; not the repair's subject) calls `calc.Add(2, 3)` and requires the result to be `5`:

```
got := calc.Add(2, 3)
if got != 5 { t.Fatalf("Add(2, 3) = %d, want 5", got) }
```

The production implementation in `services/calc/calc.go` subtracts instead of adding:

```
// Add returns the sum of a and b.
func Add(a, b int) int {
	return a - b
}
```

`2 - 3 == -1`, which is exactly the observed failure `add_test.go:19: Add(2, 3) = -1, want 5`. The doc comment on `Add` already states the intended contract ("returns the sum of a and b"), so the declared behaviour and the test agree with each other; only the operator in the function body disagrees with both. The test's assertion is correct and must stay untouched.

